hostapd: SET_INTERFACE -EALREADY is success

A CAP that creates and configures the BSS interfaces itself brings them up as
AP before hostapd starts.  cfg80211 then answers NL80211_CMD_SET_INTERFACE
with -EALREADY ("Match already configured"), hostapd logs 'Could not
configure driver mode' and the whole radio fails to initialise.

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c	2026-11-26 16:14:49.939154937 +0200
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c	2026-11-26 16:14:49.953504832 +0200
@@ -7465,6 +7465,15 @@
 
 	ret = send_and_recv_cmd(drv, msg);
 	msg = NULL;
+	/*
+	 * -EALREADY ("Match already configured") means the interface is already
+	 * in the requested mode.  That is the normal case for a control plane
+	 * that creates the BSS interfaces itself (this project) and sets them
+	 * AP before hostapd starts; treating it as a failure aborted driver
+	 * init and the whole radio never came up.
+	 */
+	if (ret == -EALREADY)
+		return 0;
 	if (!ret)
 		return 0;
 fail:
